mission "The Captain's Other Journal"
    name "The Captain's Other Journal"
    description "Bring the logbook to a shipwright who can identify the strange timber and copper fastenings."
    source "Puerto Cielo"
    destination "Port Azure"
    reward 1850
    speaker offer "Master Shipwright Edda"
    speaker visit "Master Shipwright Edda"
    speaker complete "Master Shipwright Edda"
    to offer
        has "The Wreck of the Saint Oria: done"
    on offer
        conversation
            `Master Shipwright Edda has cleared a bench for the Saint Oria's logbook. Beside it lie samples of unfamiliar timber and copper fastenings recovered from the wreck.`
            `Edda turns one of the copper fittings over in a calloused hand. "I can tell you what wood a ship is built from by the smell when you cut it. This timber is not from any yard I know, and those fastenings follow a pattern I have never seen."`
            choice
                `"Let us see where this trail leads. I am in."`
                    accept
                `"You are choosing your words carefully. Why?"`
                    goto details
                `"I cannot spare the risk or the men."`
                    close
            label details
                `Edda clears a space beside the logbook. "Bring the book and the samples together. The repairs and materials may tell us where the ship was built—or what it carried."`
                choice
                    `"Then I will see it done. No more delays."`
                        accept
                    `"I will not be persuaded. Farewell."`
                        close
    on accept
        log "Accepted The Captain's Other Journal. Bring the logbook to a shipwright who can identify the strange timber and copper fastenings."
    on visit
        conversation
            `At Port Azure, Edda compares the logbook with the timber and fittings. The construction details point to a place absent from official charts. "This was no ordinary expedition ship," Edda says. "Someone built it for a journey they did not intend to record."`
    on complete
        conversation
            `Edda wraps the samples in canvas. "I can identify the work, if not the yard. Keep these with the logbook. Together they may tell the next shipwright where the Saint Oria was meant to go."`
        log "Completed The Captain's Other Journal. Received 1850 gold. Bring the logbook to a shipwright who can identify the strange timber and copper fastenings."
